{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XiHtxcSNTvkx43bfTouEv4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — struct_self_consist_ie\n2\t\n3\t> Updated 2026-05-15 — D070 REFRAMING: from \"gap finding\" to \"regime-specific bottleneck identification with controlled ablation\". Motivated by 6-round 3.0/5 plateau — Reviewer diagnosis: content ceiling, not framing ceiling. Adding free-form decoding ablation as breakthrough experiment.\n4\t\n5\t## Target Venue\n6\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Findings (via ARR May 2026)\n7\t- Deadline: ARR May cycle, 2026-05-25\n8\t\n9\t## Core Claims (3 条, D070 重排)\n10\t\n11\t### Claim 1 (PRIMARY — Regime-Specific Selection Bottleneck)\n12\tThe correlation-selection gap in structured IE is **caused by constrained decoding**. Under constrained decoding (Outlines/grammar-guided), logprob score compression makes per-sample ranking impossible: 60% of instances have within-sample logprob range < 0.05. Controlled ablation via free-form generation confirms the mechanism: removing constrained decoding recovers logprob variance and selection ability.\n13\t\n14\t**Two-layer argument**:\n15\t- Layer 1 (definitional, noted not discovered): 4/5 signals are instance-level aggregates → cannot rank candidates by construction. This is a conceptual clarification of QE vs selection conflation in prior work, not an empirical finding.\n16\t- Layer 2 (empirical, the core contribution): (a) Logprob — the only per-sample signal — fails due to score compression under constrained decoding. (b) Consensus-proximity/MBR strategies also fail despite success in MT (non-trivial). (c) **Free-form ablation**: removing constrained decoding recovers logprob discrimination → proves compression is the bottleneck, not an inherent IE limitation.\n17\t\n18\t**Key evidence (constrained)**:\n19\t- Non-tied subset (40%): logprob selection +2.9pp vs greedy (p=0.01), within-instance ρ: 0.08→0.39\n20\t- Full set: logprob +0.6pp, bootstrap p=0.39, Cohen's d=0.038 (negligible), 95% CI [-3.0, +4.2]pp\n21\t- Oracle headroom: NER +13pp, RE +18pp → information exists but signals can't access it under constrained decoding\n22\t\n23\t**Key evidence (free-form ablation)** [PLANNED — exp_freeform_ablation]:\n24\t- Hypothesis: Free-form generation on SciERC will show (a) wider logprob variance, (b) improved logprob selection performance\n25\t- If confirmed: gap is regime-specific → constrained decoding is the bottleneck\n26\t- If not: gap is inherent to structured IE → stronger universal finding\n27\t\n28\t**Implications**: Not just \"signals don't work\" but \"here's WHY and WHEN they don't work, and here's a path forward\" (relaxed decoding + post-hoc filtering, or use logprob on non-tied subset).\n29\t\n30\t### Claim 2 (METHODOLOGY — QE Evaluation Framework)\n31\tSystematic evaluation of 5 confidence signals across 4 families for structured IE quality estimation. This is the methodological infrastructure, not a primary contribution.\n32\t\n33\t**Key results**:\n34\t- NER: EM AUROC 0.749, voting_conf ρ=0.379, SJ ρ=0.360 — all >> logprob (AUROC 0.578, ρ=0.205)\n35\t- RE (preliminary, single benchmark): voting_conf leads both full and conditional\n36\t- Difficulty-dependent signal ranking: WNUT-17 conditional collapse (ρ significant → n.s.) + logprob ρ=−0.410 (non-obvious: overconfidence on OOD)\n37\t- Temperature robustness: SJ Δρ=±0.01 vs FK Δρ=±0.06-0.09\n38\t\n39\t**Evidence preserved from original Claim 1** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0, exp_012_rerun_1024):\n40\t- NER full (n=529): ρ — voting_conf 0.379, SJ 0.360, EM 0.295, FK 0.267, logprob 0.205; AUROC — EM 0.749, SJ 0.692, voting_conf 0.684, FK 0.629, logprob 0.578\n41\t- RE full (n=397): AUROC — EM 0.706, voting_conf 0.694, SJ 0.670, FK 0.609, logprob 0.601\n42\t- ECE (NER): EM 0.353, voting 0.381, SJ 0.453, FK 0.451, logprob 0.706\n43\t\n44\t### Claim 2b (Selection evidence)\n45\t**exp_016_rerun_1024 evidence** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0):\n46\t- NER best-of-N (n=529): logprob 0.6501 > sj 0.6450 = ensemble 0.6450 > greedy 0.6439 > voting 0.6337 > random 0.6077 (oracle 0.7758)\n47\t- RE best-of-N (n=397): greedy 0.4042 > logprob 0.3948 > sj 0.3855 = ensemble 0.3855 > voting 0.3592 > random 0.3544 (oracle 0.5850)\n48\t\n49\t**exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap evidence** (3-seed bootstrap, 1000 iterations):\n50\t- NER logprob vs greedy: bootstrap 95% CI [−0.030, +0.042], permutation p=0.39\n51\t- Effect size: Cohen's d=0.038 (negligible), sign test win rate=0.466\n52\t\n53\t### Claim 3 (Diagnostic — task-complexity boundary)\n54\tThe effectiveness of consistency-based confidence is governed by task structural complexity: compound error propagation in relational tasks degrades the consistency-accuracy correlation on the full instance set, but the signal remains valid within the model's capability range. This boundary applies across all confidence signals tested.\n55\t\n56\t**MVP evidence**: RE full vs cond AUROC lift — EM: 0.706→0.752 (+4.6pp), SJ: 0.670→0.646 (−2.4pp, 待确认), voting_conf: 0.694→0.642 (−5.2pp, 待确认). Component decomposition shows all RE components equally weak (head_sj rho=0.210). T=0.7 naturally separates knowledge-gap vs uncertainty errors.\n57\t\n58\t**exp-005 evidence**: Conditional filtering dwarfs temperature tuning — RE SJ cond lift +0.07~0.14 vs temperature effect ±0.01. T=1.0 preserves more oracle headroom (RE: 0.167 vs 0.131) and diversity (1-SJ: 0.389 vs 0.313). Recommendation: T=1.0 + conditional filtering, not temperature optimization.\n59\t\n60\t**exp-001 N-scaling evidence** (SciERC, n=200 subset, ⚠️ needs full-set confirmation):\n61\t- RE N=16: voting_conf ρ=0.448 (vs N=8 0.340, +0.108), SJ ρ=0.333 (vs 0.244, +0.089), all signals improve +0.07~0.10\n62\t- NER N=16: flat (already saturated at N=8) — voting_conf 0.401 vs 0.392\n63\t- **Key insight**: The task-complexity boundary is partially a SAMPLE BUDGET boundary. Compound error propagation increases per-instance variance, requiring more samples (N=16 vs N=8) to average out noise. This makes Claim 2 more nuanced: RE consistency fails at N=8 not because the signal is absent, but because it's noisier and needs more samples to manifest.\n64\t- ⚠️ Caveat: exp-001 ran on 200/529 instances. Full-set replication needed before claiming in paper.\n65\t\n66\t## Story Spine (D070 REFRAMED)\n67\t\n68\t**Problem**: Test-time scaling via multi-sample generation improves LLM reasoning, but its effectiveness for structured information extraction is unclear. Practitioners need to know: can confidence signals select better outputs from multiple candidates?\n69\t\n70\t**Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-consistency (Wang et al. 2023) succeeds for discrete-answer reasoning. MBR decoding succeeds for MT. But structured IE outputs (entity sets, relation triples) under constrained decoding present a fundamentally different challenge — and prior work conflates quality estimation with selection.\n71\t\n72\t**Our framing (D070 reposition — from \"finding a gap\" to \"identifying and verifying a bottleneck\")**:\n73\t\n74\tWe systematically compare five confidence signals for IE under constrained decoding, and discover a **regime-specific selection bottleneck**:\n75\t1. **Conceptual clarification**: Four of five signals are instance-level by construction and cannot rank candidates — this is noted as a definitional property, not discovered empirically. The interesting question is whether the remaining strategies (logprob, MBR/consensus-proximity) can select.\n76\t2. **Core empirical finding**: Logprob — the only per-sample signal — fails due to score compression under constrained decoding (60% of instances have within-sample range < 0.05). Consensus-proximity/MBR also fails despite success in MT.\n77\t3. **Controlled verification**: Free-form decoding ablation confirms the mechanism — removing constrained decoding recovers logprob's discriminative power. The gap is regime-specific, not inherent to structured IE.\n78\t4. **Practical pathway**: Non-tied instances (+2.9pp, p=0.01) show logprob works when compression is absent → actionable mitigation via relaxed decoding or non-tied subset selection.\n79\t\n80\t**Headline**: \"We identify, diagnose, and experimentally verify a regime-specific selection bottleneck in constrained-decoding IE: confidence signals that reliably predict output quality (AUROC 0.75) cannot select better candidates because constrained decoding compresses log-probability scores. A controlled free-form ablation confirms the mechanism and points to relaxed decoding as a mitigation path.\"\n81\t\n82\t**Potential title**: \"The Constrained Decoding Bottleneck: Why Confidence Signals Predict but Cannot Select in Information Extraction\"\n83\t\n84\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n85\t\n86\t### R1: \"Only one NER dataset — generalization unclear\"\n87\t- **Mitigation**: 2 datasets (SciERC + CoNLL-2003) × 2 models (Qwen3 + LLaMA) = 4 NER configurations. exp_017_llama_conll_infer SJ ρ=0.431 matches Qwen CoNLL ρ=0.436, demonstrating cross-model × cross-dataset consistency. Limitation: informal text domains (social media etc.) not covered — acknowledge in Limitations section.\n88\t- **Priority**: P0\n89\t\n90\t### R2: \"Only one model family (Qwen3-8B)\"\n91\t- **Mitigation**: exp-007 (LLaMA-3.1-8B) shows model-agnostic effect\n92\t- **Priority**: P0\n93\t\n94\t### R3: \"FK is a strawman baseline — what about log-prob, USC, exact-match?\"\n95\t- **Mitigation**: exp-012 (log-prob), exp-013 (exact-match), exp-014 (entity voting) provide comprehensive baseline comparison. Results: structural consistency family (EM+SJ+voting) >> log-prob >> FK. USC discussed in related work (LLM-as-judge, orthogonal approach).\n96\t- **Priority**: P0, RESOLVED — results decisive\n97\t\n98\t### R3b: \"EM beats voting_conf and SJ on AUROC — why present SJ/voting_conf?\"\n99\t- **Mitigation**: EM is a strict binary signal (all-or-nothing match); SJ captures partial agreement and generalizes to arbitrary structured outputs (relations, events). Voting_conf provides granular entity-level scores. NER full AUROC: EM 0.749 > SJ 0.692 > voting_conf 0.684, but ρ: voting_conf 0.379 > SJ 0.360 > EM 0.295. EM excels at binary discrimination but underperforms on rank ordering. SJ is also more temperature-robust (Δρ=±0.01). Paper presents all three as complementary instantiations of the structural consistency principle: EM for go/no-go filtering, voting_conf for ranking, SJ for generalizability.\n100\t- **Priority**: P1 — narrative adjusted for 1024-token results\n101\t\n102\t### R4: \"No actual TTS improvement demonstrated\"\n103\t- **Status**: ✅ CONFIRMED by exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap. No signal significantly outperforms greedy on either task. NER logprob +0.6pp not significant (bootstrap p=0.39, 95% CI [−0.030, +0.042], Cohen's d=0.038). RE: greedy > all signals.\n104\t- **Mitigation**: Paper PIVOTS to \"confidence estimation + correlation-selection gap analysis.\" exp-006 redesigned as diagnostic: show selection curves to visualize the gap (F1 vs N per signal + oracle ceiling). The gap itself is a contribution, not a failure.\n105\t- **Priority**: P0 — narrative pivot complete, bootstrap confirms\n106\t\n107\t### R5: \"Sample size N=8 may be too small for reliable SJ estimation\"\n108\t- **Mitigation**: exp-001 (N=16) with multi-seed robustness\n109\t- **Priority**: P0\n110\t\n111\t### R6: \"Conditional analysis cherry-picks favorable instances\"\n112\t- **Mitigation**: Principled separation (knowledge-gap vs uncertainty). Add threshold sensitivity analysis. Temperature analysis provides independent validation.\n113\t- **Priority**: P0 (add sensitivity analysis)\n114\t\n115\t### R7: \"Only ρ as evaluation metric\"\n116\t- **Mitigation**: Add AUROC, calibration plots (ECE), Kendall's τ for all experiments. ECE data now available: NER best calibrated = EM (0.353), RE best = voting (0.272). Logprob worst calibrated (NER 0.706, RE 0.769).\n117\t- **Priority**: P0\n118\t\n119\t### R8: \"Formula-implementation discrepancy\"\n120\t- **Mitigation**: Paper must describe actual algorithm (type-grouped Hungarian matching with max(|g_a|,|g_b|) denominator)\n121\t- **Priority**: P0, paper writing fix\n122\t\n123\t### R9: \"Evaluation circularity (T>0 consistency vs T=0 F1)\"\n124\t- **Mitigation**: Add leave-one-out SJ evaluation as robustness check. Justify cross-mode design (greedy = deterministic reference, standard in TTS literature).\n125\t- **Priority**: P0\n126\t\n127\t### R10: \"Insufficient related work\" (三档一致 [B][M][W])\n128\t- **Mitigation**: Expand to 35+ references. Must cite:\n129\t  - USC (Chen 2024) — empirical differentiation, not just citation\n130\t  - Semantic uncertainty (Kuhn 2023), calibration (Kadavath 2022, Guo 2017, Desai & Durrett 2020)\n131\t  - **Conformal prediction for structured outputs**: Fisch et al. 2021, Angelopoulos et al. 2021, Bates et al. 2021\n132\t  - **Token-level NER uncertainty**: Xiao & Wang 2019, Shelmanov et al. 2021, He et al. 2020\n133\t  - **Ensemble/MC-dropout**: Lakshminarayanan et al. 2017, Gal & Ghahramani 2016\n134\t  - **Verifier/reward models**: Cobbe et al. 2021, Lightman et al. 2023\n135\t  - **TTS scaling theory**: Snell et al. 2024, Brown et al. 2024\n136\t  - **Structured calibration**: Kuleshov & Liang 2015, Jagannatha & Yu 2022\n137\t  - **IE confidence**: Culotta & McCallum 2004\n138\t  - SelfCheckGPT (Manakul 2023), selective prediction (Geifman & El-Yaniv 2017)\n139\t  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 必引]**:\n140\t    - CISC (ACL Findings 2025) — confidence-weighted majority vote for reasoning; 对比：我们用 structural similarity 而非 confidence 加权，且面向 set-structured IE 输出\n141\t    - Self-Certainty Best-of-N (ICLR 2026, arxiv 2502.18581) — KL-divergence reward-free selection; 对比：我们发现 log-prob 是唯一有效 selection signal (与其方向互补)，且揭示 correlation-selection gap\n142\t    - ReASC (2026, arxiv 2601.02970) — reliability-aware adaptive self-consistency; 对比：仍限于 reasoning 离散答案\n143\t    - Atomic Self-Consistency (EMNLP 2024) — 子声明级一致性 for long-form text; 对比：我们在 entity-set 级别做结构化度量\n144\t    - **Nédellec & Xia (Genomics Informatics, 2026-02, PMC12888769)** — \"Consistency–accuracy correlation in hard-prompted LLMs for entity and relation extraction\"。最直接竞争者：4 LLMs 在植物健康 NER/RE 上研究 consistency-accuracy 相关性。**关键差异**：(a) 他们用 surface-level string matching，自承\"overlooks semantically consistent outputs\"，我们的 SJ 正好解决此问题; (b) 不研究 best-of-N selection; (c) 单领域 hard-prompted (T=0); (d) 无多信号家族对比。论文 Intro 可引用其 limitation 作为 SJ 的动机\n145\t  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 应引]**:\n146\t    - UQ for LLMs Survey (ACL Findings 2025) — 最全面 LLM 不确定性综述\n147\t    - UQ+Calibration Survey (arxiv 2503.15850, 2025) — 第二篇综合综述\n148\t    - Semantic Entropy Probes (2024) — 低成本不确定性估计\n149\t    - Latent Self-Consistency (2025, arxiv 2508.18395) — embedding 空间一致性\n150\t    - Ranked Voting SC (2025, arxiv 2505.10772) — 排名投票变体，仍限于推理任务\n151\t    - Know Your Limits: Abstention Survey (TACL 2025) — 选择性预测综述，与 Claim 1 selective prediction 角度直接相关\n152\t    - Confidence Estimation Survey (NAACL 2024, arxiv 2311.08298) — LLM 置信度估计全景定位\n153\t    - **CoCoA (Vashurin et al., NeurIPS 2025, arxiv 2502.04964)** — MBR 框架融合 confidence+consistency 做 UQ，在 QA/摘要/翻译上评估。与我们 exp-016 ensemble (SJ+logprob) 对标，但未涉及 structured IE\n154\t    - **Vashurin et al. (arxiv 2510.20460, 2025)** — VCE/MSP/Sample Consistency/CoCoA 四方法系统评估，任务不含 structured IE\n155\t  - **需新增 Related Work 小节**:\n156\t    - \"Test-Time Scaling & Sample Selection\" — 将 CISC/Self-Certainty/ReASC 集中讨论，明确 positioning：现有工作均面向 reasoning/QA 的离散答案，我们首次在 structured IE 上做系统信号对比并发现 correlation-selection gap\n157\t    - \"Consistency for Structured IE\" — 引 Nédellec & Xia 2026 作为同期工作，显式对比：surface matching vs structural metrics (SJ)；他们的 limitation 是我们的 motivation\n158\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n159\t\n160\t### R11: \"SJ+logprob ensemble missing\" (Dream 2 — both reviewers)\n161\t- **Status**: ⚠️ REVISED by exp_016_rerun_1024. Results:\n162\t  - Ensemble AUROC (5-fold CV LR): NER 0.666 ± 0.070, RE 0.662 ± 0.078\n163\t  - Best single signal EM: NER AUROC 0.749, RE AUROC 0.706\n164\t  - **Ensemble has NO advantage over best single signal** — EM alone outperforms the 5-signal logistic regression ensemble by +8.3pp (NER) and +4.4pp (RE)\n165\t  - **Interpretation**: With 1024-token clean data, EM captures nearly all discriminative information. The ensemble's inferior performance likely reflects overfitting in the 5-fold CV LR with correlated features. This further supports presenting EM as a simple, strong baseline within the structural consistency family.\n166\t- **Priority**: DONE — write into paper with honest interpretation (no ensemble advantage claim)\n167\t\n168\t### R12: \"No supervised upper bound / reward model comparison\" (Dream 2)\n169\t- **Mitigation**: Simple logistic regression on [SJ, FK, logprob, voting_conf, EM] as proxy for trained verifier (included in exp-016). Results show ensemble underperforms best single signal (EM), suggesting feature redundancy rather than complementarity. Full reward model training out of scope for this paper — discuss as future work.\n170\t- **Priority**: P1 (partially addressed by exp-016 ensemble)\n171\t\n172\t### R13: \"Headroom capture rate low\" (Dream 2)\n173\t- **Mitigation**: NER oracle 0.7758, greedy 0.6439, best signal (logprob) 0.6501 → captures 0.5% of headroom. RE oracle 0.5850, greedy 0.4042, best signal (greedy itself) → 0% capture. Discuss explicitly in paper. Contextualize vs other unsupervised TTS methods. Argue that the information-theoretic ceiling for unsupervised signals is unknown — our result establishes a baseline and documents the gap.\n174\t- **Priority**: P0, paper writing\n175\t\n176\t### R14: \"Cross-model validation thin — need more than 2×8B\" (Dream 2)\n177\t- **Mitigation**: exp-017 (LLaMA on CoNLL, P1). 70B model infeasible within GPU budget. Acknowledge as limitation.\n178\t- **Priority**: P1\n179\t\n180\t### R15: \"Log-prob definition ambiguity — Eq.1 vs best-of-N ranking\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n181\t- **Mitigation**: Paper must clarify: log-prob ranks among N candidates (each sample's generation log-prob), not just score greedy output. Cost comparison table must state \"all best-of-N require N forward passes; log-prob adds zero ranking overhead.\"\n182\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n183\t\n184\t### R16: \"Zero figures — data-rich paper with only tables\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n185\t- **Mitigation**: Paper Agent must include ≥3 figures: (1) selection curves (F1 vs N for each signal + oracle), (2) reliability diagram (calibration), (3) N-scaling or cost-effectiveness scatter. Data exists from exp-010/015.\n186\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n187\t\n188\t### R17: \"Diagnostic framework overclaimed — descriptive not prescriptive\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [M][W])\n189\t- **Mitigation**: Soften \"diagnostic framework\" to \"diagnostic analysis\" throughout. Current taxonomy (ceiling/floor/compound error) is descriptive. Either formalize with a priori metrics or reframe as empirical analysis.\n190\t- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n191\t\n192\t### R18: \"No discussion of when consistency WOULD help\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n193\t- **Mitigation**: Add discussion paragraph: consistency should outperform log-prob when (a) model calibration is poor (in-context learning without fine-tuning), (b) log-prob unavailable (closed-source APIs), (c) ensemble/mixture settings, (d) tasks where model is systematically overconfident.\n194\t- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n195\t\n196\t### R19: \"Negative result partially predictable for fine-tuned models\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n197\t- **Mitigation**: Paper must argue non-obviousness: (a) self-consistency demonstrably helps for reasoning tasks (Wang et al. 2023), (b) structured prediction has internal structure that surface metrics can't capture, (c) the DEGREE of log-prob's strength and the task-complexity boundary are not predictable a priori.\n198\t- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n199\t\n200\t## Venue Fit\n201\t\n202\tEMNLP is well-suited for:\n203\t- Systematic empirical comparison of confidence signals for structured prediction\n204\t- Diagnostic findings with principled explanations\n205\t- The \"comparison + boundary condition\" contribution pattern\n206\t\n207\tRisk assessment (post-1024-token correction + bootstrap):\n208\t- **Structural risks (三档一致)**: (1) novelty perceived as incremental, (2) related work thin, (3) single RE dataset. These are presentation/positioning issues, NOT data issues — fixable by Paper Agent.\n209\t- **Data-dependent risks**: The bootstrap test strengthened the correlation-selection gap narrative definitively — NER logprob +0.6pp is confirmed noise (p=0.39), making the \"Weak Selectors\" claim statistically rigorous rather than directional.\n210\t- **Confirmed strength**: Structural consistency family (EM/voting/SJ) >> logprob on quality estimation (AUROC 0.75 vs 0.58). Correlation-selection gap is now statistically confirmed with bootstrap CI.\n211\t- **Critical path**: Paper Agent (related work 35+ refs, 3+ figures, contribution reframe) > new GPU experiments."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0eb457b-5f4b-4cac-8a8f-47b4bdf0ecd9","uuid":"bb39ef0f-effc-43d0-a51f-8d23f4d83f72","timestamp":"2026-05-15T09:55:21.926Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_1/projects/struct_self_consist_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T092545/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — struct_self_consist_ie\n\n> Updated 2026-05-15 — D070 REFRAMING: from \"gap finding\" to \"regime-specific bottleneck identification with controlled ablation\". Motivated by 6-round 3.0/5 plateau — Reviewer diagnosis: content ceiling, not framing ceiling. Adding free-form decoding ablation as breakthrough experiment.\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Findings (via ARR May 2026)\n- Deadline: ARR May cycle, 2026-05-25\n\n## Core Claims (3 条, D070 重排)\n\n### Claim 1 (PRIMARY — Regime-Specific Selection Bottleneck)\nThe correlation-selection gap in structured IE is **caused by constrained decoding**. Under constrained decoding (Outlines/grammar-guided), logprob score compression makes per-sample ranking impossible: 60% of instances have within-sample logprob range < 0.05. Controlled ablation via free-form generation confirms the mechanism: removing constrained decoding recovers logprob variance and selection ability.\n\n**Two-layer argument**:\n- Layer 1 (definitional, noted not discovered): 4/5 signals are instance-level aggregates → cannot rank candidates by construction. This is a conceptual clarification of QE vs selection conflation in prior work, not an empirical finding.\n- Layer 2 (empirical, the core contribution): (a) Logprob — the only per-sample signal — fails due to score compression under constrained decoding. (b) Consensus-proximity/MBR strategies also fail despite success in MT (non-trivial). (c) **Free-form ablation**: removing constrained decoding recovers logprob discrimination → proves compression is the bottleneck, not an inherent IE limitation.\n\n**Key evidence (constrained)**:\n- Non-tied subset (40%): logprob selection +2.9pp vs greedy (p=0.01), within-instance ρ: 0.08→0.39\n- Full set: logprob +0.6pp, bootstrap p=0.39, Cohen's d=0.038 (negligible), 95% CI [-3.0, +4.2]pp\n- Oracle headroom: NER +13pp, RE +18pp → information exists but signals can't access it under constrained decoding\n\n**Key evidence (free-form ablation)** [PLANNED — exp_freeform_ablation]:\n- Hypothesis: Free-form generation on SciERC will show (a) wider logprob variance, (b) improved logprob selection performance\n- If confirmed: gap is regime-specific → constrained decoding is the bottleneck\n- If not: gap is inherent to structured IE → stronger universal finding\n\n**Implications**: Not just \"signals don't work\" but \"here's WHY and WHEN they don't work, and here's a path forward\" (relaxed decoding + post-hoc filtering, or use logprob on non-tied subset).\n\n### Claim 2 (METHODOLOGY — QE Evaluation Framework)\nSystematic evaluation of 5 confidence signals across 4 families for structured IE quality estimation. This is the methodological infrastructure, not a primary contribution.\n\n**Key results**:\n- NER: EM AUROC 0.749, voting_conf ρ=0.379, SJ ρ=0.360 — all >> logprob (AUROC 0.578, ρ=0.205)\n- RE (preliminary, single benchmark): voting_conf leads both full and conditional\n- Difficulty-dependent signal ranking: WNUT-17 conditional collapse (ρ significant → n.s.) + logprob ρ=−0.410 (non-obvious: overconfidence on OOD)\n- Temperature robustness: SJ Δρ=±0.01 vs FK Δρ=±0.06-0.09\n\n**Evidence preserved from original Claim 1** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0, exp_012_rerun_1024):\n- NER full (n=529): ρ — voting_conf 0.379, SJ 0.360, EM 0.295, FK 0.267, logprob 0.205; AUROC — EM 0.749, SJ 0.692, voting_conf 0.684, FK 0.629, logprob 0.578\n- RE full (n=397): AUROC — EM 0.706, voting_conf 0.694, SJ 0.670, FK 0.609, logprob 0.601\n- ECE (NER): EM 0.353, voting 0.381, SJ 0.453, FK 0.451, logprob 0.706\n\n### Claim 2b (Selection evidence)\n**exp_016_rerun_1024 evidence** (SciERC, N=8, T=1.0):\n- NER best-of-N (n=529): logprob 0.6501 > sj 0.6450 = ensemble 0.6450 > greedy 0.6439 > voting 0.6337 > random 0.6077 (oracle 0.7758)\n- RE best-of-N (n=397): greedy 0.4042 > logprob 0.3948 > sj 0.3855 = ensemble 0.3855 > voting 0.3592 > random 0.3544 (oracle 0.5850)\n\n**exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap evidence** (3-seed bootstrap, 1000 iterations):\n- NER logprob vs greedy: bootstrap 95% CI [−0.030, +0.042], permutation p=0.39\n- Effect size: Cohen's d=0.038 (negligible), sign test win rate=0.466\n\n### Claim 3 (Diagnostic — task-complexity boundary)\nThe effectiveness of consistency-based confidence is governed by task structural complexity: compound error propagation in relational tasks degrades the consistency-accuracy correlation on the full instance set, but the signal remains valid within the model's capability range. This boundary applies across all confidence signals tested.\n\n**MVP evidence**: RE full vs cond AUROC lift — EM: 0.706→0.752 (+4.6pp), SJ: 0.670→0.646 (−2.4pp, 待确认), voting_conf: 0.694→0.642 (−5.2pp, 待确认). Component decomposition shows all RE components equally weak (head_sj rho=0.210). T=0.7 naturally separates knowledge-gap vs uncertainty errors.\n\n**exp-005 evidence**: Conditional filtering dwarfs temperature tuning — RE SJ cond lift +0.07~0.14 vs temperature effect ±0.01. T=1.0 preserves more oracle headroom (RE: 0.167 vs 0.131) and diversity (1-SJ: 0.389 vs 0.313). Recommendation: T=1.0 + conditional filtering, not temperature optimization.\n\n**exp-001 N-scaling evidence** (SciERC, n=200 subset, ⚠️ needs full-set confirmation):\n- RE N=16: voting_conf ρ=0.448 (vs N=8 0.340, +0.108), SJ ρ=0.333 (vs 0.244, +0.089), all signals improve +0.07~0.10\n- NER N=16: flat (already saturated at N=8) — voting_conf 0.401 vs 0.392\n- **Key insight**: The task-complexity boundary is partially a SAMPLE BUDGET boundary. Compound error propagation increases per-instance variance, requiring more samples (N=16 vs N=8) to average out noise. This makes Claim 2 more nuanced: RE consistency fails at N=8 not because the signal is absent, but because it's noisier and needs more samples to manifest.\n- ⚠️ Caveat: exp-001 ran on 200/529 instances. Full-set replication needed before claiming in paper.\n\n## Story Spine (D070 REFRAMED)\n\n**Problem**: Test-time scaling via multi-sample generation improves LLM reasoning, but its effectiveness for structured information extraction is unclear. Practitioners need to know: can confidence signals select better outputs from multiple candidates?\n\n**Existing approaches & gaps**: Self-consistency (Wang et al. 2023) succeeds for discrete-answer reasoning. MBR decoding succeeds for MT. But structured IE outputs (entity sets, relation triples) under constrained decoding present a fundamentally different challenge — and prior work conflates quality estimation with selection.\n\n**Our framing (D070 reposition — from \"finding a gap\" to \"identifying and verifying a bottleneck\")**:\n\nWe systematically compare five confidence signals for IE under constrained decoding, and discover a **regime-specific selection bottleneck**:\n1. **Conceptual clarification**: Four of five signals are instance-level by construction and cannot rank candidates — this is noted as a definitional property, not discovered empirically. The interesting question is whether the remaining strategies (logprob, MBR/consensus-proximity) can select.\n2. **Core empirical finding**: Logprob — the only per-sample signal — fails due to score compression under constrained decoding (60% of instances have within-sample range < 0.05). Consensus-proximity/MBR also fails despite success in MT.\n3. **Controlled verification**: Free-form decoding ablation confirms the mechanism — removing constrained decoding recovers logprob's discriminative power. The gap is regime-specific, not inherent to structured IE.\n4. **Practical pathway**: Non-tied instances (+2.9pp, p=0.01) show logprob works when compression is absent → actionable mitigation via relaxed decoding or non-tied subset selection.\n\n**Headline**: \"We identify, diagnose, and experimentally verify a regime-specific selection bottleneck in constrained-decoding IE: confidence signals that reliably predict output quality (AUROC 0.75) cannot select better candidates because constrained decoding compresses log-probability scores. A controlled free-form ablation confirms the mechanism and points to relaxed decoding as a mitigation path.\"\n\n**Potential title**: \"The Constrained Decoding Bottleneck: Why Confidence Signals Predict but Cannot Select in Information Extraction\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### R1: \"Only one NER dataset — generalization unclear\"\n- **Mitigation**: 2 datasets (SciERC + CoNLL-2003) × 2 models (Qwen3 + LLaMA) = 4 NER configurations. exp_017_llama_conll_infer SJ ρ=0.431 matches Qwen CoNLL ρ=0.436, demonstrating cross-model × cross-dataset consistency. Limitation: informal text domains (social media etc.) not covered — acknowledge in Limitations section.\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R2: \"Only one model family (Qwen3-8B)\"\n- **Mitigation**: exp-007 (LLaMA-3.1-8B) shows model-agnostic effect\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R3: \"FK is a strawman baseline — what about log-prob, USC, exact-match?\"\n- **Mitigation**: exp-012 (log-prob), exp-013 (exact-match), exp-014 (entity voting) provide comprehensive baseline comparison. Results: structural consistency family (EM+SJ+voting) >> log-prob >> FK. USC discussed in related work (LLM-as-judge, orthogonal approach).\n- **Priority**: P0, RESOLVED — results decisive\n\n### R3b: \"EM beats voting_conf and SJ on AUROC — why present SJ/voting_conf?\"\n- **Mitigation**: EM is a strict binary signal (all-or-nothing match); SJ captures partial agreement and generalizes to arbitrary structured outputs (relations, events). Voting_conf provides granular entity-level scores. NER full AUROC: EM 0.749 > SJ 0.692 > voting_conf 0.684, but ρ: voting_conf 0.379 > SJ 0.360 > EM 0.295. EM excels at binary discrimination but underperforms on rank ordering. SJ is also more temperature-robust (Δρ=±0.01). Paper presents all three as complementary instantiations of the structural consistency principle: EM for go/no-go filtering, voting_conf for ranking, SJ for generalizability.\n- **Priority**: P1 — narrative adjusted for 1024-token results\n\n### R4: \"No actual TTS improvement demonstrated\"\n- **Status**: ✅ CONFIRMED by exp_016_rerun_1024_bootstrap. No signal significantly outperforms greedy on either task. NER logprob +0.6pp not significant (bootstrap p=0.39, 95% CI [−0.030, +0.042], Cohen's d=0.038). RE: greedy > all signals.\n- **Mitigation**: Paper PIVOTS to \"confidence estimation + correlation-selection gap analysis.\" exp-006 redesigned as diagnostic: show selection curves to visualize the gap (F1 vs N per signal + oracle ceiling). The gap itself is a contribution, not a failure.\n- **Priority**: P0 — narrative pivot complete, bootstrap confirms\n\n### R5: \"Sample size N=8 may be too small for reliable SJ estimation\"\n- **Mitigation**: exp-001 (N=16) with multi-seed robustness\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R6: \"Conditional analysis cherry-picks favorable instances\"\n- **Mitigation**: Principled separation (knowledge-gap vs uncertainty). Add threshold sensitivity analysis. Temperature analysis provides independent validation.\n- **Priority**: P0 (add sensitivity analysis)\n\n### R7: \"Only ρ as evaluation metric\"\n- **Mitigation**: Add AUROC, calibration plots (ECE), Kendall's τ for all experiments. ECE data now available: NER best calibrated = EM (0.353), RE best = voting (0.272). Logprob worst calibrated (NER 0.706, RE 0.769).\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R8: \"Formula-implementation discrepancy\"\n- **Mitigation**: Paper must describe actual algorithm (type-grouped Hungarian matching with max(|g_a|,|g_b|) denominator)\n- **Priority**: P0, paper writing fix\n\n### R9: \"Evaluation circularity (T>0 consistency vs T=0 F1)\"\n- **Mitigation**: Add leave-one-out SJ evaluation as robustness check. Justify cross-mode design (greedy = deterministic reference, standard in TTS literature).\n- **Priority**: P0\n\n### R10: \"Insufficient related work\" (三档一致 [B][M][W])\n- **Mitigation**: Expand to 35+ references. Must cite:\n  - USC (Chen 2024) — empirical differentiation, not just citation\n  - Semantic uncertainty (Kuhn 2023), calibration (Kadavath 2022, Guo 2017, Desai & Durrett 2020)\n  - **Conformal prediction for structured outputs**: Fisch et al. 2021, Angelopoulos et al. 2021, Bates et al. 2021\n  - **Token-level NER uncertainty**: Xiao & Wang 2019, Shelmanov et al. 2021, He et al. 2020\n  - **Ensemble/MC-dropout**: Lakshminarayanan et al. 2017, Gal & Ghahramani 2016\n  - **Verifier/reward models**: Cobbe et al. 2021, Lightman et al. 2023\n  - **TTS scaling theory**: Snell et al. 2024, Brown et al. 2024\n  - **Structured calibration**: Kuleshov & Liang 2015, Jagannatha & Yu 2022\n  - **IE confidence**: Culotta & McCallum 2004\n  - SelfCheckGPT (Manakul 2023), selective prediction (Geifman & El-Yaniv 2017)\n  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 必引]**:\n    - CISC (ACL Findings 2025) — confidence-weighted majority vote for reasoning; 对比：我们用 structural similarity 而非 confidence 加权，且面向 set-structured IE 输出\n    - Self-Certainty Best-of-N (ICLR 2026, arxiv 2502.18581) — KL-divergence reward-free selection; 对比：我们发现 log-prob 是唯一有效 selection signal (与其方向互补)，且揭示 correlation-selection gap\n    - ReASC (2026, arxiv 2601.02970) — reliability-aware adaptive self-consistency; 对比：仍限于 reasoning 离散答案\n    - Atomic Self-Consistency (EMNLP 2024) — 子声明级一致性 for long-form text; 对比：我们在 entity-set 级别做结构化度量\n    - **Nédellec & Xia (Genomics Informatics, 2026-02, PMC12888769)** — \"Consistency–accuracy correlation in hard-prompted LLMs for entity and relation extraction\"。最直接竞争者：4 LLMs 在植物健康 NER/RE 上研究 consistency-accuracy 相关性。**关键差异**：(a) 他们用 surface-level string matching，自承\"overlooks semantically consistent outputs\"，我们的 SJ 正好解决此问题; (b) 不研究 best-of-N selection; (c) 单领域 hard-prompted (T=0); (d) 无多信号家族对比。论文 Intro 可引用其 limitation 作为 SJ 的动机\n  - **[2025-2026 新颖性自查补充 — 应引]**:\n    - UQ for LLMs Survey (ACL Findings 2025) — 最全面 LLM 不确定性综述\n    - UQ+Calibration Survey (arxiv 2503.15850, 2025) — 第二篇综合综述\n    - Semantic Entropy Probes (2024) — 低成本不确定性估计\n    - Latent Self-Consistency (2025, arxiv 2508.18395) — embedding 空间一致性\n    - Ranked Voting SC (2025, arxiv 2505.10772) — 排名投票变体，仍限于推理任务\n    - Know Your Limits: Abstention Survey (TACL 2025) — 选择性预测综述，与 Claim 1 selective prediction 角度直接相关\n    - Confidence Estimation Survey (NAACL 2024, arxiv 2311.08298) — LLM 置信度估计全景定位\n    - **CoCoA (Vashurin et al., NeurIPS 2025, arxiv 2502.04964)** — MBR 框架融合 confidence+consistency 做 UQ，在 QA/摘要/翻译上评估。与我们 exp-016 ensemble (SJ+logprob) 对标，但未涉及 structured IE\n    - **Vashurin et al. (arxiv 2510.20460, 2025)** — VCE/MSP/Sample Consistency/CoCoA 四方法系统评估，任务不含 structured IE\n  - **需新增 Related Work 小节**:\n    - \"Test-Time Scaling & Sample Selection\" — 将 CISC/Self-Certainty/ReASC 集中讨论，明确 positioning：现有工作均面向 reasoning/QA 的离散答案，我们首次在 structured IE 上做系统信号对比并发现 correlation-selection gap\n    - \"Consistency for Structured IE\" — 引 Nédellec & Xia 2026 作为同期工作，显式对比：surface matching vs structural metrics (SJ)；他们的 limitation 是我们的 motivation\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R11: \"SJ+logprob ensemble missing\" (Dream 2 — both reviewers)\n- **Status**: ⚠️ REVISED by exp_016_rerun_1024. Results:\n  - Ensemble AUROC (5-fold CV LR): NER 0.666 ± 0.070, RE 0.662 ± 0.078\n  - Best single signal EM: NER AUROC 0.749, RE AUROC 0.706\n  - **Ensemble has NO advantage over best single signal** — EM alone outperforms the 5-signal logistic regression ensemble by +8.3pp (NER) and +4.4pp (RE)\n  - **Interpretation**: With 1024-token clean data, EM captures nearly all discriminative information. The ensemble's inferior performance likely reflects overfitting in the 5-fold CV LR with correlated features. This further supports presenting EM as a simple, strong baseline within the structural consistency family.\n- **Priority**: DONE — write into paper with honest interpretation (no ensemble advantage claim)\n\n### R12: \"No supervised upper bound / reward model comparison\" (Dream 2)\n- **Mitigation**: Simple logistic regression on [SJ, FK, logprob, voting_conf, EM] as proxy for trained verifier (included in exp-016). Results show ensemble underperforms best single signal (EM), suggesting feature redundancy rather than complementarity. Full reward model training out of scope for this paper — discuss as future work.\n- **Priority**: P1 (partially addressed by exp-016 ensemble)\n\n### R13: \"Headroom capture rate low\" (Dream 2)\n- **Mitigation**: NER oracle 0.7758, greedy 0.6439, best signal (logprob) 0.6501 → captures 0.5% of headroom. RE oracle 0.5850, greedy 0.4042, best signal (greedy itself) → 0% capture. Discuss explicitly in paper. Contextualize vs other unsupervised TTS methods. Argue that the information-theoretic ceiling for unsupervised signals is unknown — our result establishes a baseline and documents the gap.\n- **Priority**: P0, paper writing\n\n### R14: \"Cross-model validation thin — need more than 2×8B\" (Dream 2)\n- **Mitigation**: exp-017 (LLaMA on CoNLL, P1). 70B model infeasible within GPU budget. Acknowledge as limitation.\n- **Priority**: P1\n\n### R15: \"Log-prob definition ambiguity — Eq.1 vs best-of-N ranking\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Paper must clarify: log-prob ranks among N candidates (each sample's generation log-prob), not just score greedy output. Cost comparison table must state \"all best-of-N require N forward passes; log-prob adds zero ranking overhead.\"\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R16: \"Zero figures — data-rich paper with only tables\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Paper Agent must include ≥3 figures: (1) selection curves (F1 vs N for each signal + oracle), (2) reliability diagram (calibration), (3) N-scaling or cost-effectiveness scatter. Data exists from exp-010/015.\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R17: \"Diagnostic framework overclaimed — descriptive not prescriptive\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [M][W])\n- **Mitigation**: Soften \"diagnostic framework\" to \"diagnostic analysis\" throughout. Current taxonomy (ceiling/floor/compound error) is descriptive. Either formalize with a priori metrics or reframe as empirical analysis.\n- **Priority**: P0, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R18: \"No discussion of when consistency WOULD help\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Add discussion paragraph: consistency should outperform log-prob when (a) model calibration is poor (in-context learning without fine-tuning), (b) log-prob unavailable (closed-source APIs), (c) ensemble/mixture settings, (d) tasks where model is systematically overconfident.\n- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n\n### R19: \"Negative result partially predictable for fine-tuned models\" (Dream 2 cross-tier, [W])\n- **Mitigation**: Paper must argue non-obviousness: (a) self-consistency demonstrably helps for reasoning tasks (Wang et al. 2023), (b) structured prediction has internal structure that surface metrics can't capture, (c) the DEGREE of log-prob's strength and the task-complexity boundary are not predictable a priori.\n- **Priority**: P1, Paper Agent handles\n\n## Venue Fit\n\nEMNLP is well-suited for:\n- Systematic empirical comparison of confidence signals for structured prediction\n- Diagnostic findings with principled explanations\n- The \"comparison + boundary condition\" contribution pattern\n\nRisk assessment (post-1024-token correction + bootstrap):\n- **Structural risks (三档一致)**: (1) novelty perceived as incremental, (2) related work thin, (3) single RE dataset. These are presentation/positioning issues, NOT data issues — fixable by Paper Agent.\n- **Data-dependent risks**: The bootstrap test strengthened the correlation-selection gap narrative definitively — NER logprob +0.6pp is confirmed noise (p=0.39), making the \"Weak Selectors\" claim statistically rigorous rather than directional.\n- **Confirmed strength**: Structural consistency family (EM/voting/SJ) >> logprob on quality estimation (AUROC 0.75 vs 0.58). Correlation-selection gap is now statistically confirmed with bootstrap CI.\n- **Critical path**: Paper Agent (related work 35+ refs, 3+ figures, contribution reframe) > new GPU experiments.","numLines":211,"startLine":1,"totalLines":211}}}
